{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The proof repeatedly lifts recursive subset facts into appended variable lists. A local append-preservation lemma removes those transitivity subproofs while retaining the special normalized-application contradiction.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  intro Hnorm\\n  have appendSubset : ∀ {a b c d : List Expression.Ident},\\n      a.Subset c → b.Subset d → (a ++ b).Subset (c ++ d) := by\\n    intro a b c d ha hb x hx\\n    simp_all\\n  induction post <;>\\n    simp [Imperative.HasVarsPure.getVars, extractOldExprVars,\\n      Lambda.LExpr.LExpr.getVars] at * <;>\\n    try simp_all\\n  case app fn e fn_ih e_ih =>\\n    unfold extractOldExprVars\\n    split\\n    · simp [Lambda.LExpr.LExpr.getVars]\\n    · rename_i Hfalse\\n      cases Hnorm with\\n      | app Hfn He Hshape =>\\n        exfalso\\n        specialize Hshape (by constructor)\\n        cases Hshape\\n        exact Hfalse rfl\\n    · cases Hnorm with\\n      | app Hfn He Hshape =>\\n        exact appendSubset (fn_ih Hfn) (e_ih He)\\n  case abs ih =>\\n    cases Hnorm with\\n    | abs H => exact ih H\\n  case quant tr_ih e_ih =>\\n    cases Hnorm with\\n    | quant Htr He => exact appendSubset (tr_ih Htr) (e_ih He)\\n  case ite c_ih t_ih e_ih =>\\n    cases Hnorm with\\n    | ite Hc Ht He =>\\n      exact appendSubset (c_ih Hc) (appendSubset (t_ih Ht) (e_ih He))\\n  case eq e1_ih e2_ih =>\\n    cases Hnorm with\\n    | eq H1 H2 => exact appendSubset (e1_ih H1) (e2_ih H2)\"}"}}
